  "prefLabel": "Mec 104.02 Custodian of Records; Inspection and Copies of Records",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 104.02 Custodian of Records; Inspection and Copies of Records.\n\n(a) The office of professional licensure and certification shall be the custodian of the board's records, and shall make available, upon request, those records which are subject to public inspection under RSA 91-A.\n\n(b) Persons desiring to inspect or obtain copies of board records shall identify as specifically as possible the information being sought.\n\n(c) If records are requested which contain both public information and information exempt from disclosure pursuant to RSA 91-A or other law, the board shall redact the information exempt from disclosure and provide the remaining information, unless otherwise ordered by a court of competent jurisdiction.\n\nSource. #10798, eff 3-18-15; ss by #13483, eff 1-9-23 (formerly Saf-Mec 104.02) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 100); #14408, eff 10-17-25\n\nAPPENDIX\n\nAPPENDIX II\n\nINCORPORATION BY REFERENCE INFORMATION\n\nRule | Title | Obtain at:\n\nMec 102.02 | Standards of Apprenticeship - CFR 29 (Amended March 11, 2020) | National Archives, Code of Federal Regulations Online: eCFR :: 29 CFR Part 29 -- Labor Standards for the Registration of Apprenticeship Programs Cost: None\n\nMec 102.02 | Standards of Apprenticeship - CFR 30 (Amended December 16, 2016) | National Archives, Code of Federal Regulations Online: eCFR :: 29 CFR Part 29 -- Labor Standards for the Registration of Apprenticeship Programs Cost: None",
